.TH ps 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
ps \- report process status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ps
[\fB\-aAeNrlf\fR] [\fB\-p\fI pidlist\fR] [\fB\-t\fI ttylist\fR] [\fB\-u\fI uidlist\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ps
prints a line for each process it is asked about.  With no options it
shows your own processes on this terminal.
.PP
The information comes from
.BR /dev/proc ,
which the kernel provides; there is no
.B /proc
filesystem.
.SH SELECTION
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-e
Every process.
.TP
.B \-a
Every process that has a terminal.
.TP
.B \-r
Only processes running or ready to run, rather than sleeping.
.TP
.BI \-p " pidlist"
Only these process ids.
.TP
.BI \-t " ttylist"
Only processes on these terminals.
.TP
.BI \-U " uidlist"
Only processes owned by these users.
.B \-u
means the same as
.BR \-U ,
which is a deviation from the standard.
.TP
.B \-N
Invert the selection: show what the other options did
.I not
select.
.PP
Lists are comma separated.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.TP
.B \-f
Full listing: uid, pid, ppid, C, start time, tty, time and command.
.TP
.B \-l
Long listing: adds flags, state, priority, nice, address, size and the
wait channel.
.SH STATES
.TP
.B R
Running, or ready to run.
.TP
.B S
Sleeping.
.TP
.B D
Waiting on I/O, and not to be interrupted.
.TP
.B T
Stopped.
.TP
.B Z
A zombie, waiting for its parent to collect it.
.TP
.B F
In the middle of a fork.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# ps
# ps -ef
# ps -l -p 1
# ps -u root
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (1),
.BR killall (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR uptime (1)
